WEBVTT

00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:05.770
They caught up to Kyoto Fushimi with 
500 meters to the mountain line!

00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:08.670
Since Sohoku and Hakone Academy 
are keeping their eyes on them,

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:10.740
they'll be crushed immediately 
if they try to get ahead.

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:13.950
And since Onoda can't participate 
in the finish line sprint,

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:14.990
Sohoku effectively has one member.

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:18.490
Hakone Academy's the only team with 
two cards left for the finish line.

00:00:18.490 --> 00:00:22.340
Hakone Academy has an overwhelming advantage!

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:35.470
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:01:53.770 --> 00:01:55.420
Yikes!

00:01:54.570 --> 00:01:59.070
<i>LINE.20 King of the Mountain</i>

00:01:55.770 --> 00:01:58.050
What's with these guys' intensity?

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:00.800
Imaizumi and Shinkai!

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:03.260
My mountain line!

00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:07.690
With 400 meters remaining,
 they're trying to steal my dream—

00:02:03.970 --> 00:02:05.390
<b><i>Road Race</i>
Distance to Day 2
 Mountain Checkpoint</b>

00:02:07.690 --> 00:02:10.470
Shut up, Mizuta-kun.

00:02:10.470 --> 00:02:14.220
No one cares about your stupid dream.

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:14.840
Huh?

00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:19.000
No one cares about the insignificant 
King of the Mountain title.

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:19.530
Insignificant?

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:23.660
No one's fighting for that.

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:25.660
<i>What? Really?</i>

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:30.280
You can fall behind now.

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:31.160
Huh? What's going on?

00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:34.230
Your job is finished.

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:40.430
Hey!

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:37.640
<i>King of the Mountain?</i>

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:39.240
<i>Overwhelming disadvantage?</i>

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:40.430
<i>Over?</i>

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:42.240
<i>Really?</i>

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:46.180
<i>Is that really what's happening?</i>

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:48.980
<i>They caught up,</i>

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:54.730
<i>and Hakone Academy has an overwhelming 
advantage just before the finish line?</i>

00:02:55.590 --> 00:02:58.790
<i>Am I really out of options?</i>

00:02:59.350 --> 00:03:03.560
<i>No. This situation...</i>

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:05.530
<i>is just the opposite!</i>

00:03:05.530 --> 00:03:08.520
<i>We're simultaneously before the finish line</i>

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:11.550
<i>and 400 meters away from the mountain line.</i>

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:13.920
<i>Maybe...</i>

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:16.120
Huh? What?

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:18.760
Who said you could fall behind?

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:20.220
Huh? You did...

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:24.270
You shouldn't give up on your dream.

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:25.100
What? My dream?

00:03:25.550 --> 00:03:27.850
Go get the mountain line.

00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:28.640
Huh?

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:30.350
Go, Zaku!

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:35.560
Kyoto Fushimi sent #112!

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:37.230
Is he going for the mountain line?

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:38.230
<i>Where did that come from?</i>

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:39.380
<i>But it's true!</i>

00:03:39.380 --> 00:03:42.740
<i>He really did have the highest hopes for me!</i>

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:44.570
<i>I'll take it,</i>

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:47.080
<i>Midousuji-kun!</i>

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:49.040
<i>What is Midousuji doing?</i>

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:51.610
<i>He'll be caught immediately at that speed.</i>

00:03:51.610 --> 00:03:52.500
<i>It's meaningless.</i>

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:57.960
<i>Or does his team really 
want the mountain line?</i>

00:03:58.730 --> 00:04:00.800
<i>This is chum.</i>

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:09.640
<i>Chum you spread to lure bait while 
fishing for a really big fish.</i>

00:04:09.990 --> 00:04:15.650
<i>I told him no one's fighting for 
the King of the Mountain title.</i>

00:04:15.650 --> 00:04:24.410
<i>But there are guys here putting on airs 
who desperately want that title.</i>

00:04:24.970 --> 00:04:30.200
<i>They won't be able to ignore this.</i>

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:31.310
200 meters left!

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:33.130
You can do it, Kyoto Fushimi!

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:38.290
<i>They won't allow themselves to be humiliated 
by losing a special number tag.</i>

00:04:38.290 --> 00:04:39.880
<i>Take the bait.</i>

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:40.840
<i>Take the bait.</i>

00:04:41.290 --> 00:04:42.730
<i>Take the bait!</i>

00:04:46.230 --> 00:04:47.390
After him, Yuto.

00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:49.890
Don't let him take the red number tag.

00:04:49.890 --> 00:04:52.140
<i>He took the bait!</i>

00:04:52.730 --> 00:04:54.390
Ashikiba-san?

00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:56.720
We're coming up on the finish line.

00:04:56.720 --> 00:04:59.320
We shouldn't be worrying 
about colored number tags.

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:01.400
Just go and get it.

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:04.930
At this distance, it'll have 
to be an all-out attack.

00:05:04.930 --> 00:05:06.130
If I do that now,

00:05:06.130 --> 00:05:09.740
I won't be able to assist you during the 
finish line sprint that's coming up.

00:05:10.060 --> 00:05:12.870
We made it to this point with an advantage.

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:16.620
We'd be losing one of
 Hakone Academy's two cards.

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:18.170
Go, Yuto.

00:05:19.370 --> 00:05:21.880
There's no need for us to 
disadvantage ourselves.

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:26.180
Let Kyoto Fushimi have the red number tag.

00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:28.340
What's gotten into you, Ashikiba-san?

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:30.040
I see.

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:33.060
You're still a first-year.

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:34.220
You don't understand.

00:05:35.970 --> 00:05:38.310
We are Hakone Academy.

00:05:38.970 --> 00:05:42.690
We fight with pride!

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:44.030
Wait!

00:05:44.030 --> 00:05:45.150
I'll go!

00:05:45.520 --> 00:05:46.440
Ashikiba-san!

00:05:46.440 --> 00:05:49.660
If Kyoto Fushimi's ace 
makes a move, handle it!

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:51.370
Third-year Ashikiba-san is...

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:53.620
<i>Just as planned!</i>

00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:54.870
He's fast!

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:57.190
He caught up in an instant!

00:05:57.670 --> 00:06:01.540
<i>Hakone Academy has won all 
the number tags so far.</i>

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:04.920
<i>They have their pride as champions.</i>

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:08.170
<i>Naturally, they want the 
mountain title as well.</i>

00:06:08.170 --> 00:06:10.970
<i>And they'll end up losing something important</i>

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:14.610
<i>because they're so concerned 
with something so insignificant.</i>

00:06:14.610 --> 00:06:16.180
<i>As far as I'm concerned,</i>

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:21.310
<i>colored number tags are useless scraps 
of paper before the finish line.</i>

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:23.570
<i>He actually took the bait.</i>

00:06:24.030 --> 00:06:30.150
<i>I thought they'd send 
their assist Shinkai-kun,</i>

00:06:30.930 --> 00:06:34.300
<i>but it's their ace who impatiently left.</i>

00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:39.920
<i>My last-minute plan might result in 
Hakone Academy losing one of its cards.</i>

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:46.000
<i>I don't know what happened,
 but it's exactly what I wanted!</i>

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:49.510
<i>No, more!</i>

00:06:51.480 --> 00:06:55.350
<i>Hakone Academy's Ashikiba is the 
second day's King of the Mountain!</i>

00:06:55.350 --> 00:06:58.130
<i>He caught up in an instant 
with his all-out climb!</i>

00:06:57.170 --> 00:06:59.020
Hakone Academy is amazing!

00:06:59.020 --> 00:07:00.780
You did it, Ashikiba-san!

00:07:00.780 --> 00:07:02.610
We're the best!

00:07:02.610 --> 00:07:04.640
First the sprint, now the mountains!

00:07:04.640 --> 00:07:06.820
Now take the finish line!

00:07:07.250 --> 00:07:08.820
<i>An all-out climb...</i>

00:07:10.310 --> 00:07:12.700
<i>Now I'm useless.</i>

00:07:13.430 --> 00:07:15.740
<i>Isn't that right, Yuto?</i>

00:07:16.250 --> 00:07:17.790
<i>The other riders are raising their pace</i>

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:20.850
<i>and crossing the mountain line 
one after another.</i>

00:07:20.850 --> 00:07:23.750
<i>Just past the gate is the finish line!</i>

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:27.220
Damn that lanky Hakone Academy guy!

00:07:27.220 --> 00:07:29.210
He took my mountain line!

00:07:29.210 --> 00:07:34.600
Midousuji-kun, I rode as 
hard as I could, but he—

00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:36.760
Huh? Hey, wait...

00:07:40.730 --> 00:07:43.480
Congratulations, King of the Mountain.

00:07:43.930 --> 00:07:49.220
We didn't stand a chance 
against your all-out attack.

00:07:49.220 --> 00:07:51.030
It was amazing.

00:07:51.030 --> 00:07:56.070
We wanted the title so badly, 
we even sent our captain.

00:07:57.620 --> 00:08:00.250
I can't believe you took it from us.

00:08:01.490 --> 00:08:04.000
Should you have done that as the ace?

00:08:04.410 --> 00:08:07.300
Should you have used up your legs?

00:08:07.300 --> 00:08:12.630
The finish line is at the bottom of the hill.

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:18.930
<i>He sent Mizuta to use up 
one of Hakone Academy's cards.</i>

00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:21.960
<i>Hakone Academy had the advantage,</i>

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:24.390
<i>but now they're disadvantaged.</i>

00:08:24.920 --> 00:08:26.070
Imaizumi-kun...

00:08:26.850 --> 00:08:30.150
Why didn't Ashikiba-san stay ahead?

00:08:30.150 --> 00:08:31.570
He let us catch up so easily.

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:33.210
We don't have far to go,

00:08:33.210 --> 00:08:36.240
but he determined we'd catch him with 
our numbers even if he stayed ahead.

00:08:36.710 --> 00:08:42.750
If it's unlikely he'll stay ahead, it's smarter 
to rejoin the group, rest his legs,

00:08:43.270 --> 00:08:45.330
and stay behind his assistant.

00:08:45.740 --> 00:08:50.340
You must've thought you could 
take it easily, Hakone Academy.

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:54.630
You thought you'd pretend you 
didn't want the mountain line,

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:57.180
approach the line with the pack,

00:08:57.570 --> 00:09:02.520
and send someone at the last second 
to take the number tag easily.

00:08:58.990 --> 00:09:02.410
Mountain Line

00:09:04.170 --> 00:09:05.770
Lucky you.

00:09:06.130 --> 00:09:08.820
Things turned out differently.

00:09:08.820 --> 00:09:11.530
It seems like you paid a high price.

00:09:11.530 --> 00:09:13.940
But your pride, is it?

00:09:15.590 --> 00:09:18.660
Something so easily blown away,

00:09:18.660 --> 00:09:20.780
but you protected it.

00:09:20.780 --> 00:09:22.850
Hey, you—

00:09:23.490 --> 00:09:25.410
Yeah, we're glad.

00:09:26.570 --> 00:09:27.850
We have no regrets.

00:09:28.930 --> 00:09:30.630
The atmosphere's changing.

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:32.960
I like those eyes.

00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:35.150
They're the eyes of one who won't collapse.

00:09:35.150 --> 00:09:37.220
Someone who won't lose.

00:09:37.220 --> 00:09:39.470
At least try to keep your spirits up.

00:09:39.960 --> 00:09:44.100
The real battle for the 
finish line starts now!

00:09:46.470 --> 00:09:47.660
<i>The race for the finish.</i>

00:09:47.660 --> 00:09:49.220
Fall back, Sakamichi.

00:09:49.220 --> 00:09:51.440
<i>Imaizumi-kun's moving up?</i>

00:09:51.440 --> 00:09:53.920
Thanks for pulling until now.

00:09:53.920 --> 00:09:54.990
From here on out,

00:09:55.460 --> 00:09:56.740
it's my job.

00:09:58.050 --> 00:10:01.490
Okay! Good luck, Imaizumi-kun!

00:10:01.490 --> 00:10:03.620
<b>Day 2
Mountain Line</b>

00:10:02.340 --> 00:10:03.620
Man.

00:10:04.980 --> 00:10:06.830
What a roller coaster.

00:10:07.450 --> 00:10:09.750
This is why I love road racing.

00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:14.050
There's no telling who will 
win the second day, either.

00:10:14.050 --> 00:10:18.970
<b>Elevation</b>

00:10:15.460 --> 00:10:17.490
Don't let them beat you, Sohoku.

00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:23.010
Gunma Prefecture's Treasure 
of the West, Mount Haruna.

00:10:23.010 --> 00:10:25.860
1,449 meters above sea level.

00:10:25.860 --> 00:10:29.700
Its summit is a large volcanic crater.

00:10:30.170 --> 00:10:32.680
And at the bottom of that caldera is

00:10:32.680 --> 00:10:37.900
Lake Haruna and the beautiful, 
conical Mount Haruna-Fuji.

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:39.320
<b>No Thru Traffic</b>

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:43.480
And at the Mount Haruna-Fuji
 Ropeway parking lot,

00:10:43.480 --> 00:10:47.380
along the road circling
 Lake Haruna, stands the gate.

00:10:49.860 --> 00:10:53.170
This is the Inter-High's 
second day finish line.

00:10:53.510 --> 00:10:56.040
I heard the lead pack's already 
crossed the mountain line.

00:10:56.040 --> 00:10:58.010
I'm impressed Sohoku caught up.

00:10:58.010 --> 00:11:01.770
Just before the mountain line, their climber

00:11:01.770 --> 00:11:04.430
pulled their second-year ace 
Imaizumi to the lead pack.

00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:05.760
Imaizumi?

00:11:06.790 --> 00:11:08.700
Imaizumi! Imaizumi!

00:11:08.700 --> 00:11:10.180
What's gotten into you, Sugimoto?

00:11:10.180 --> 00:11:10.940
Are you going to faint?

00:11:10.940 --> 00:11:13.280
You did it. You did a great job.

00:11:13.280 --> 00:11:14.230
Does your stomach hurt?

00:11:14.710 --> 00:11:15.960
You're almost there.

00:11:15.960 --> 00:11:18.110
You can do it. You can do it.

00:11:18.110 --> 00:11:20.990
You can do it, Imaizumi!

00:11:18.920 --> 00:11:20.990
Now he's shouting!

00:11:20.990 --> 00:11:23.410
Don't you care what other people will think?

00:11:23.410 --> 00:11:25.030
There's no way he can hear you!

00:11:25.470 --> 00:11:27.120
He will.

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:28.370
Huh?

00:11:28.840 --> 00:11:30.250
That feeling will reach him.

00:11:30.890 --> 00:11:33.080
He'll receive that feeling

00:11:33.570 --> 00:11:35.960
and ride with all his might.

00:11:37.490 --> 00:11:39.800
<i>You can do it, Imaizumi-kun.</i>

00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:43.390
<i>And well done, Onoda-kun.</i>

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:45.860
<i>They're fast.</i>

00:11:45.860 --> 00:11:48.300
<i>They're so fast on the downhill.</i>

00:11:48.300 --> 00:11:51.520
<i>Since I'm not good on downhills, 
I'm slowly falling behind.</i>

00:11:52.020 --> 00:11:54.230
<i>But it's the end!</i>

00:11:58.180 --> 00:11:59.940
Onoda, what are you doing?

00:11:59.940 --> 00:12:01.890
We still have to race tomorrow.

00:12:01.890 --> 00:12:03.170
You can fall back.

00:12:03.170 --> 00:12:05.660
Don't waste your energy.

00:12:05.660 --> 00:12:06.450
What are you—

00:12:08.570 --> 00:12:11.250
I forgot to do this.

00:12:17.500 --> 00:12:19.670
I'm entrusting my hopes to you!

00:12:19.670 --> 00:12:22.050
Do it!

00:12:22.450 --> 00:12:24.180
There are two kilometers to the finish line.

00:12:24.180 --> 00:12:25.760
You can do it.

00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:29.800
I know it'll be hard, but, uh...

00:12:29.800 --> 00:12:32.560
I know it'll be tough, but, uh...

00:12:30.520 --> 00:12:32.560
You think I'm that bad?

00:12:33.460 --> 00:12:35.270
I'm entrusting you with the team's hopes!

00:12:40.340 --> 00:12:42.990
You can do it, Imaizumi-kun!

00:12:42.990 --> 00:12:43.530
Yeah!

00:12:47.830 --> 00:12:51.240
<i>I left it to him, at the very end,</i>

00:12:51.730 --> 00:12:55.300
<i>the jersey the team carried this far.</i>

00:12:58.050 --> 00:13:00.310
I relaxed too much.

00:13:01.160 --> 00:13:02.920
<i>We're racing tomorrow, too.</i>

00:13:03.540 --> 00:13:05.430
<i>I have to finish today.</i>

00:13:06.410 --> 00:13:10.140
<i>We made it this far, Naruko-kun.</i>

00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:11.560
It's Naruko-san!

00:13:11.560 --> 00:13:13.670
Hey, Naruko!

00:13:13.670 --> 00:13:15.920
You're alive. Are you okay?

00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:16.930
Can you ride?

00:13:18.010 --> 00:13:19.950
Just barely.

00:13:19.950 --> 00:13:22.210
No, wait! Who do you think you're talking to?

00:13:22.210 --> 00:13:24.550
I'm Naruko the genius!

00:13:24.550 --> 00:13:25.730
<i>He rejoined the team.</i>

00:13:26.330 --> 00:13:27.300
<i>Naruko...</i>

00:13:27.730 --> 00:13:31.830
<i>He sacrificed himself to 
get Sohoku to the front.</i>

00:13:31.830 --> 00:13:34.420
Well done. You did great.

00:13:34.420 --> 00:13:36.370
Tastes like sauce.

00:13:36.370 --> 00:13:37.370
So,

00:13:37.810 --> 00:13:42.030
did hotshot catch up to them?

00:13:42.030 --> 00:13:43.080
Yeah.

00:13:43.690 --> 00:13:46.800
The lead car's board told us the situation.

00:13:47.290 --> 00:13:50.300
The lead pack pulled ahead of Onoda.

00:13:50.300 --> 00:13:54.770
Including Imaizumi, four of them 
are embroiled in the final battle!

00:13:54.770 --> 00:13:56.810
<i>The four leaders are here!</i>

00:13:57.240 --> 00:14:01.130
<i>The downhill has ended, and they're 
entering the flats around Lake Haruna.</i>

00:14:01.130 --> 00:14:03.650
<i>There's just a few hundred 
meters left to the finish line!</i>

00:14:04.040 --> 00:14:05.620
<i>Am I hearing things?</i>

00:14:05.620 --> 00:14:08.420
<i>I thought I just heard Sugimoto's voice.</i>

00:14:09.510 --> 00:14:11.620
<i>I won't let you take this, Hakone Academy.</i>

00:14:11.620 --> 00:14:13.410
I'll ride in front!

00:14:14.340 --> 00:14:17.100
<i>Hakone Academy lost their ace.</i>

00:14:17.100 --> 00:14:22.400
<i>An ace should save his last bullet 
for the finish line sprint,</i>

00:14:23.210 --> 00:14:29.050
<i>so he can fire it just before the 
finish line and push aside all others.</i>

00:14:29.990 --> 00:14:32.850
<i>That's what Midousuji-san 
and Imaizumi-san are doing.</i>

00:14:32.850 --> 00:14:36.680
<i>But Hakone Academy used ours</i>

00:14:37.320 --> 00:14:39.570
<i>to win an insignificant mountain title.</i>

00:14:41.570 --> 00:14:43.890
<i>What am I pulling for right now?</i>

00:14:44.650 --> 00:14:48.320
<i>It's like carrying a pistol 
that's out of bullets.</i>

00:14:49.080 --> 00:14:51.000
<i>This has never happened before.</i>

00:14:52.130 --> 00:14:54.170
<i>Ashikiba-san is supposed to be calm.</i>

00:14:54.170 --> 00:14:55.380
<i>He's intelligent.</i>

00:14:55.380 --> 00:14:57.490
<i>He always makes the right choice.</i>

00:14:58.330 --> 00:15:00.540
<i>He's kind and strong.</i>

00:15:01.400 --> 00:15:05.110
<i>As far as I'm concerned, he's far more 
impressive than my other seniors.</i>

00:15:05.110 --> 00:15:06.710
What is it, Yuto?

00:15:07.190 --> 00:15:08.950
Think I should cut my hair again?

00:15:09.430 --> 00:15:12.730
You're right. It's too long.

00:15:13.610 --> 00:15:16.350
No, I was just looking.

00:15:17.160 --> 00:15:20.150
You're really tall, Ashikiba-san.

00:15:20.630 --> 00:15:21.810
Ow...

00:15:22.200 --> 00:15:25.260
<i>So I respected you.</i>

00:15:25.260 --> 00:15:26.320
<i>But...</i>

00:15:26.930 --> 00:15:28.850
<i>Why, Ashikiba-san?</i>

00:15:29.270 --> 00:15:34.160
You're not someone to act
 thoughtlessly, Ashikiba-san!

00:15:34.790 --> 00:15:39.640
If we'd given up the mountain line, 
this finish line would've been ours!

00:15:39.640 --> 00:15:40.580
Easily!

00:15:40.920 --> 00:15:42.420
Face forward, Yuto.

00:15:42.760 --> 00:15:44.630
Because we're in the middle of a race?

00:15:44.630 --> 00:15:46.630
That's right. Face forward.

00:15:46.630 --> 00:15:48.050
This is pointless!

00:15:48.540 --> 00:15:51.130
Hakone Academy has spent all its bullets!

00:15:51.830 --> 00:15:53.050
I...

00:15:53.850 --> 00:15:57.600
I haven't given up on the 
mountain or finish line yet.

00:16:05.380 --> 00:16:06.930
That's the club room.

00:16:06.930 --> 00:16:08.980
I've been here once before.

00:16:12.600 --> 00:16:15.550
Hello. I'm interested in joining the team.

00:16:15.550 --> 00:16:16.410
Seriously?

00:16:16.750 --> 00:16:18.580
He's really a first-year?

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:20.070
Crazy, right?

00:16:20.070 --> 00:16:22.620
Is that true?

00:16:20.470 --> 00:16:22.620
<i>They're excited about something...</i>

00:16:22.620 --> 00:16:24.240
Shinkai-san's brother is here.

00:16:24.240 --> 00:16:26.270
What? Seriously?

00:16:26.270 --> 00:16:27.480
<i>I'll come back another day.</i>

00:16:28.390 --> 00:16:29.630
Huh?

00:16:30.810 --> 00:16:33.450
Hey, you. Wanna join the bicycle club?

00:16:33.450 --> 00:16:33.970
You a first-year?

00:16:34.890 --> 00:16:36.680
Sorry we didn't notice.

00:16:36.680 --> 00:16:39.010
We just got some big news.

00:16:39.010 --> 00:16:43.880
There was a god-like sprinter named 
Shinkai-san who graduated last year.

00:16:43.880 --> 00:16:46.310
His brother is...

00:16:47.690 --> 00:16:49.400
It's him!

00:16:49.400 --> 00:16:51.610
What? You found his brother?

00:16:51.610 --> 00:16:52.690
You're right.

00:16:52.690 --> 00:16:54.040
Whoa, their faces look so similar.

00:16:54.040 --> 00:16:56.270
It's Shinkai-san. He looks so young.

00:16:55.730 --> 00:16:58.530
<i>You don't need to point...</i>

00:16:56.270 --> 00:16:57.690
He's a little Shinkai-san.

00:16:57.690 --> 00:16:59.030
The rumors were true.

00:16:59.500 --> 00:17:01.550
Could you stop pointing at me?

00:17:01.550 --> 00:17:02.820
Do you do the ka-pow pose, too?

00:17:02.820 --> 00:17:05.300
I'm not Hayato-kun. I'm Yuto.

00:17:06.890 --> 00:17:08.310
Haven't you had enough?

00:17:08.310 --> 00:17:10.280
My brother has nothing to do with this.

00:17:10.280 --> 00:17:11.860
I'm my own person.

00:17:12.850 --> 00:17:15.380
Why are you taking pictures of me?!

00:17:22.390 --> 00:17:23.770
Things are awkward.

00:17:24.130 --> 00:17:26.900
Since that incident, yeah.

00:17:27.250 --> 00:17:31.110
In any case, Yuto still hasn't 
apologized to second-year Haraguchi.

00:17:31.110 --> 00:17:33.190
I told him it wasn't his fault.

00:17:33.190 --> 00:17:36.250
Even pandas get mad if you 
take pictures of them.

00:17:36.250 --> 00:17:39.100
When I heard Shinkai-san's 
brother was coming,

00:17:39.100 --> 00:17:42.240
I thought the club would handle it better.

00:17:42.240 --> 00:17:45.000
That incident has completely 
turned things upside down.

00:17:45.610 --> 00:17:48.460
Now we're treating him with kid gloves.

00:17:49.080 --> 00:17:56.190
<i>They did approach him as a group, and go on
 about what a god and star his brother was.</i>

00:17:56.190 --> 00:17:59.050
<i>I can see why it annoys him.</i>

00:17:59.560 --> 00:18:02.770
<i>Touichirou doesn't know 
how to handle him, either.</i>

00:18:02.770 --> 00:18:04.090
<i>Of course he doesn't.</i>

00:18:04.090 --> 00:18:06.810
<i>He's Shinkai-san's brother.</i>

00:18:06.810 --> 00:18:12.250
I ran into Yuto in the hallway, 
but he didn't even say hi.

00:18:12.250 --> 00:18:14.750
Maybe he doesn't recognize us yet.

00:18:14.750 --> 00:18:15.890
What?

00:18:15.890 --> 00:18:18.510
Shinkai-san spoke pretty highly of me.

00:18:18.510 --> 00:18:19.680
It came as a shock.

00:18:19.680 --> 00:18:21.560
<i>This is Hakone Academy.</i>

00:18:21.560 --> 00:18:23.190
<i>Only the strong ride.</i>

00:18:23.190 --> 00:18:23.990
<i>That's all we ask.</i>

00:18:24.900 --> 00:18:28.360
<i>Being rebellious isn't a bad thing at all.</i>

00:18:28.870 --> 00:18:36.450
<i>But if he's chosen for the Inter-High team,
 the others won't accept it.</i>

00:18:37.380 --> 00:18:39.330
Damn it! Someone's catching up!

00:18:39.330 --> 00:18:40.410
Shinkai?

00:18:40.410 --> 00:18:41.910
He passed the second-years?

00:18:41.910 --> 00:18:44.510
This is a practice session for 
Hakone Academy's best climbers!

00:18:44.510 --> 00:18:45.930
Raise the pace, Kaneyan!

00:18:45.930 --> 00:18:47.380
I know, Shino!

00:18:47.380 --> 00:18:50.400
He may be his brother, 
but we can't hold back!

00:18:50.770 --> 00:18:54.400
It's time to go.

00:18:55.540 --> 00:18:57.160
On this steep incline?

00:18:57.820 --> 00:19:00.780
And you call yourselves third-years.

00:19:01.210 --> 00:19:02.840
Talk about lame.

00:19:02.840 --> 00:19:04.660
You're losing to a first-year.

00:19:05.090 --> 00:19:07.120
Isn't that right?

00:19:07.120 --> 00:19:09.540
Is that a yes?

00:19:10.960 --> 00:19:16.370
Damn. When I heard Shinkai-san's brother 
was a climber instead of a sprinter,

00:19:16.370 --> 00:19:18.120
I underestimated him.

00:19:18.120 --> 00:19:21.400
He's a real climber!

00:19:24.850 --> 00:19:27.160
You're surprising everyone, Yuto.

00:19:28.120 --> 00:19:30.140
Oh, uh...

00:19:30.140 --> 00:19:32.210
Oh, Ashikiba-san?

00:19:33.460 --> 00:19:36.760
<i>This is the guy everyone 
thinks is an airhead.</i>

00:19:37.320 --> 00:19:40.140
<i>He's a third-year and the ace.</i>

00:19:40.140 --> 00:19:42.410
<i>Why is this guy the ace?</i>

00:19:42.410 --> 00:19:44.340
<i>Come to think of it,
 we've never spoken before.</i>

00:19:44.950 --> 00:19:46.970
You're tall.

00:19:46.970 --> 00:19:48.690
Your bangs must be annoying.

00:19:48.690 --> 00:19:50.390
Why don't you cut them?

00:19:51.030 --> 00:19:53.170
Did beating the third-years go to your head?

00:19:54.710 --> 00:19:56.920
Oh, no. Sorry.

00:19:57.420 --> 00:20:00.570
Should you be acting like that 
in front of a third-year?

00:20:00.570 --> 00:20:03.350
You're talking to me with your back 
turned and a drink in your hand.

00:20:03.350 --> 00:20:05.760
Oh, you're right.

00:20:06.730 --> 00:20:08.390
<i>What's with this guy?</i>

00:20:09.290 --> 00:20:13.750
<i>The team calls him an airhead, 
but his words carry a strange weight.</i>

00:20:14.360 --> 00:20:16.710
When you joined the team,

00:20:16.710 --> 00:20:21.570
you were told to ask second- and third-years 
for advice after practicing with them.

00:20:22.490 --> 00:20:23.560
Why aren't you doing that?

00:20:23.560 --> 00:20:25.300
<i>So he's lecturing me?</i>

00:20:25.300 --> 00:20:29.380
I don't need advice from 
people weaker than me.

00:20:29.380 --> 00:20:32.210
Did anyone criticize your attitude?

00:20:32.210 --> 00:20:33.840
Not really.

00:20:33.840 --> 00:20:36.630
If anything, they said I should be confident.

00:20:37.120 --> 00:20:41.300
No one wants to criticize 
you because of Shinkai-san.

00:20:42.690 --> 00:20:47.350
Isn't that what you want 
to shake off the most?

00:20:49.890 --> 00:20:53.430
Get on your bike, first-year Shinkai Yuto.

00:20:53.430 --> 00:20:54.940
Huh?

00:20:55.400 --> 00:21:01.900
I really don't like hearing that about guys 
I've been riding with for three years.

00:21:02.950 --> 00:21:05.820
Let's race to the top of that hill.

00:21:06.730 --> 00:21:08.320
I'll crush you.

00:21:14.260 --> 00:21:15.250
Fine.

00:21:16.660 --> 00:21:19.000
Third-year Ashikiba-san.

00:21:19.770 --> 00:21:21.830
I'll crush you back.

00:22:58.170 --> 00:23:00.610
Brain freeze!

00:23:01.270 --> 00:23:03.310
That always happens to you, Onoda-kun.

00:23:03.310 --> 00:23:05.020
It's because you don't eat slowly.

00:23:05.330 --> 00:23:09.750
Watch how experienced shaved ice 
eater Sugimoto Terufumi eats.

00:23:11.670 --> 00:23:13.780
You got brain freeze, too?!

00:23:13.780 --> 00:23:15.640
You guys are too predictable.

00:23:15.640 --> 00:23:16.440
Watch this.

00:23:16.440 --> 00:23:18.470
This is the Speed Eater of Naniwa!

00:23:24.690 --> 00:23:26.200
Huh? Wh-What?

00:23:26.200 --> 00:23:28.130
I'm not doing anything special.

00:23:29.880 --> 00:23:31.510
Wow, lame.

00:23:34.130 --> 00:23:36.600
<i>It's that sound again...</i>

00:23:36.830 --> 00:23:39.980
<i>NEXT LINE  Limiter</i>

00:23:39.980 --> 00:23:44.980
This is a work of fiction. All characters and organizations
 appearing in this work are fictional. In this work,
 characters sometimes engage in dangerous activities.
 While riding bicycles on actual roads,
 please follow all traffic laws and ride safely.

00:23:44.980 --> 00:23:50.250
<b>Don't miss the next episode</b>
